import{_ as a,o as t,c as s,a3 as i}from"./chunks/framework.B8xISX-C.js";const p=JSON.parse('{"title":"Pictures and sound","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Pictures and sound"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"guide/pictures-and-sound.md","filePath":"guide/pictures-and-sound.md"}'),o={name:"guide/pictures-and-sound.md"};function r(l,e,n,d,c,h){return t(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i(`<h1 id="pictures-and-sound" tabindex="-1">Pictures and sound <a class="header-anchor" href="#pictures-and-sound" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Pictures and sound&quot;">​</a></h1><p>This page covers how a mod supplies pictures and sound: roles, file formats and sizes.</p><h2 id="roles" tabindex="-1">Roles <a class="header-anchor" href="#roles" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Roles&quot;">​</a></h2><p><code>assets/roles.json</code> connects your files to the places the game draws and plays them. Its <code>&quot;$schema&quot;</code> is <code>&quot;carina-roles/1&quot;</code>. Each row of <code>roles</code> is <code>{ &quot;role&quot;: &quot;&lt;role id&gt;&quot;, &quot;file&quot;: &quot;assets/&lt;path&gt;&quot; }</code>:</p><div class="language-json vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">json</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">{</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">  &quot;role&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">: </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;menus.title.backdrop&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">,</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;">  &quot;file&quot;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">: </span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">&quot;assets/title.png&quot;</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">}</span></span></code></pre></div><p>A role is a place in the game: a title backdrop, a galaxy star field, a race portrait, a sound effect, a music cue. <a href="/carina-mod-template/reference/roles">Roles</a> lists every role with its kind, exact size and frame grammar. A file of the wrong size or kind is refused on import, with the role named.</p><p>A role is one of three things:</p><ul><li>A base role, which the mod overrides.</li><li>A picture of a race the package adds.</li><li>A new role named <code>&lt;namespace&gt;.&lt;name&gt;</code>.</li></ul><p>Packages stack in load order. A later package&#39;s role or text replaces an earlier one&#39;s.</p><h2 id="files" tabindex="-1">Files <a class="header-anchor" href="#files" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Files&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Pictures</strong> are PNG or WebP. Each image is the exact size of its role. At most 4096 pixels a side, 16 Mpx per image and 64 Mpx per package.</li><li><strong>Sound</strong> is Ogg, Opus or Vorbis. Music is at most 300 seconds and an effect at most 10, by the file&#39;s own length.</li><li>An <code>.m4a</code> twin is optional: the same role with <code>.m4a</code> added, for browsers that do not play Ogg. One case requires it: a race without an art base must bring <code>music.race.&lt;race key&gt;</code> and its <code>.m4a</code> twin.</li></ul><h2 id="races" tabindex="-1">Races <a class="header-anchor" href="#races" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Races&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A race you add either names an art base or supplies its whole contract.</p><ul><li>With an art base, <code>{ &quot;race&quot;: &quot;&lt;your race key&gt;&quot;, &quot;artBase&quot;: &quot;&lt;stock race key&gt;&quot; }</code> in <code>races</code>, every picture the race does not bring is the base race&#39;s.</li><li>Without one, the race brings every role of its contract: portraits, ambassador, emblems, council medallions, ships, colonist figures and theme music. <a href="/carina-mod-template/reference/roles">Roles</a> lists them. <a href="/carina-mod-template/examples/hollow-choir">Hollow Choir</a> does this.</li></ul><p>The numbered portrait variants of the stock Humans are not available to a race you add. The importer refuses them with <code>role-namespace</code>.</p><h2 id="buildings" tabindex="-1">Buildings <a class="header-anchor" href="#buildings" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Buildings&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A building you add is drawn on the colony lot in one of two ways, and not both:</p><ul><li>Its own atlas, the role <code>colony.lot.&lt;building key with each _ written as -&gt;</code>. It has 36 sprites, one per cell of the 6 x 6 lot, named <code>r&lt;0-5&gt;c&lt;0-5&gt;_x&lt;X&gt;_y&lt;Y&gt;</code> in the <code>frames</code> list of the role row. <a href="/carina-mod-template/reference/roles#building-lot-art">Roles: building lot art</a> gives the grammar and the screen box of every cell. <a href="/carina-mod-template/examples/prism-optics">Prism Optics</a> is the worked example.</li><li><code>artFrom</code>, which draws it like a base building: <code>{ &quot;catalog&quot;: &quot;buildings&quot;, &quot;key&quot;: &quot;&lt;your building&gt;&quot;, &quot;from&quot;: &quot;&lt;base building key&gt;&quot; }</code>.</li></ul><p>Listing both is refused with <code>art-from-twice</code>. A building with neither is not drawn on the lot.</p><h2 id="cosmetic-packs" tabindex="-1">Cosmetic packs <a class="header-anchor" href="#cosmetic-packs" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Cosmetic packs&quot;">​</a></h2><p>A package that holds only text, pictures or sound has no <code>rules</code> capability. It is a cosmetic pack.</p><ul><li>It changes nothing about the rules, so players need no agreement on it.</li><li>On the INSTALLED tab it sits under LOOK AND SOUND and has an ON/OFF switch in its row.</li><li>It does not appear in the RULES row of New Game.</li><li>Its text wins over a rules mod&#39;s text.</li></ul><p><a href="/carina-mod-template/examples/deep-field">Deep Field</a> is a cosmetic pack with backdrops and music.</p><h2 id="limits" tabindex="-1">Limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Limits&quot;">​</a></h2><p><a href="/carina-mod-template/reference/limits">Limits</a> lists the bounds: sizes, paths and the combat ship atlas frame names.</p>`,25)])])}const m=a(o,[["render",r]]);export{p as __pageData,m as default};
